<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Path A entitlements — Developer ID Application signing for direct DMG
  distribution from privycs.com. No App Store sandbox; the app runs with
  the user's full privileges and the privileged helper installs as a
  LaunchDaemon. Hardened Runtime is enabled (required for notarization
  on macOS 10.14.5+) but we relax three CS restrictions:

  - allow-jit: Wails embeds WebKit which JIT-compiles JavaScript; without
    this the WebView throws on every script-eval.

  - allow-unsigned-executable-memory: belt-and-suspenders alongside
    allow-jit for any code that mmap's RWX pages outside the JIT path
    (Go runtime traceback handler, some cgo bridges).

  - disable-library-validation: we load wireguard-go as a Go module
    (linked into the binary) plus libpcap, libxar, etc. for various
    helper paths. Library validation would refuse anything not signed
    with our team identifier; disabling it lets the Go runtime's
    dynamic loading work.

  Network entitlements: client (outbound) + server (the privileged
  helper accepts IPC connections on a Unix domain socket; technically
  not net.server but Apple bundles all socket capability under it for
  hardened-runtime auditing).

  Path B (App Store) needs a separate entitlements-appstore.plist with
  app-sandbox=true and com.apple.developer.networking.networkextension
  — see that file for the future migration scaffold.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.network.client</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.network.server</key>
    <true/>
    <!--
      Personal VPN (NEVPNManager IKEv2) — lets the app create + control
      its own IPSec VPN config in-process (replaces the dead
      .mobileconfig+AppleScript path and the Homebrew-strongSwan/swanctl
      backend). See nevpn_macos.go.

      CONFIRMED (v1.0.7.7/.8 crashed): this is a restricted/managed
      entitlement. On Developer-ID (non-App-Store) distribution AMFI
      SIGKILLs the app at launch ("CODESIGNING Taskgated Invalid
      Signature") unless an embedded provisioning profile authorizes it —
      even though Gatekeeper/notarization accept the app (spctl: accepted).
      The CI build embeds Contents/embedded.provisionprofile (macOS
      Developer ID profile for App ID com.privycs.vpn with the Personal
      VPN capability) BEFORE codesign; see desktop-release.yml. The three
      entitlements below (vpn.api + application-identifier +
      team-identifier) must be a subset of that profile's entitlements.
      The helper runs from inside the .app bundle (getHelperBinaryPath →
      os.Executable), so it finds the same embedded profile.
    -->
    <key>com.apple.developer.networking.vpn.api</key>
    <array>
        <string>allow-vpn</string>
    </array>
    <key>com.apple.application-identifier</key>
    <string>LDGP24V3Q8.com.privycs.vpn</string>
    <key>com.apple.developer.team-identifier</key>
    <string>LDGP24V3Q8</string>
</dict>
</plist>
